On Sat, Oct 25, 2014 at 3:52 AM, Gleki Arxokuna <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com>
wrote:

>
> From usability point of view: {postmxo} is infinitely harder to pronounce
> than {postmo}.
>

If it was up to me, I would disallow consonantal syllables altogether. and
change the rule for type-3 fu'ivla to CVC(C)yrC...V.

Consonantal syllables don't occur in the core lojban words
cmavo/gismu/lujvo, they were introduced for type-3 fu'ivla. but they should
have made do with what they already had instead of adding new complications.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

